   "text": "The drawing matches raltitrexed, an L-glutamic acid amide of a 5-(methylamino)thiophene-2-carbonyl group, linked through a CH2 to a 2-methylquinazolin-4(3H)-one.\n\n- **Quinazolinone:** the ring system has a methyl on C2, a ring N=C and an NH, and a C4 carbonyl. The CH2 attaches at C6 of the benzo ring.\n- **Linker:** the CH2 goes to an N-methyl nitrogen, which is bonded to C5 of the thiophene.\n- **Thiophene:** the C2 position carries a C(=O)NH amide.\n- **Glutamate:** the amide nitrogen is bonded to the \u03b1-carbon, which carries a COOH and a CH2CH2COOH chain.\n- **Stereochemistry:** the CH2 bond at the \u03b1-carbon is a wedge. With the implicit H pointing away, the sequence N \u2192 COOH \u2192 CH2 runs counterclockwise, which gives S, as in L-glutamic acid. That corresponds to N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)O.\n\nSMILES: CC1=NC2=C(C=C(CN(C)C3=CC=C(S3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C=C2)C(=O)N1"
